fresh DORA transaction immediately after boot; this is plausible NetworkManager lease-file behavior but a fresh dhclient -r/full renewal log was not captured to unambiguously prove a new lease negotiation occurred post-boot as opposed to a cached lease file being reloaded.","The ping test from node3 to 192.168.21.10 (cmd-e45a956add29460c) failed with an unusual source address (206.248.153.34) unrelated to any configured subnet; this is expected since node3 should not have a route to node2's segment through the relay (only broadcast DHCP traffic is relayed, not general routing), but it was not explicitly explained in the executor's report."]},"ttft_ms":37790,"type":"result","duration_ms":78426,"uuid":"f727e374-527d-4fd4-b298-b61694dfe230","ttft_stream_ms":2509,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":2914,"queued_turn_count":0}
